\p{In the upper drawing the large orbit is the solution of
\ref{fnip-0011}, started at #{(0,n_{R})}. The short orbit on the left
starts at #{(-50,0.2)}, a point chosen for this drawing, and ends at
the equilibrium.
\citet{Figure 3.2a, p. 54}{ermentrout2010mathematical}
is this current. In the lower drawing one orbit returns to its
starting point, and the other starts at #{(-60,0.25)}, also chosen
for this drawing, and joins it.
\citet{Figure 3.2d, pp. 54–55}{ermentrout2010mathematical}
draws one intersection of the nullclines and a curve that returns to
itself at #{I_{\mathrm{app}}=100}.}
